<div class="wb-check-options">
  <p class="wb-dialog-meta">DEX {{modifier}} · 1 reaction · once per round</p>
  {{#unless unlocked}}<p class="wb-warning">DEX 21 not reached.</p>{{/unless}}
  {{#unless armed}}<p class="wb-warning">No weapon or shield equipped.</p>{{/unless}}
  <label>Attack total<input type="number" name="target" step="any" placeholder="Optional"></label>
  <label class="wb-check-toggle"><input type="checkbox" name="ally"> Protect an ally</label>
  <label class="wb-check-toggle" data-tooltip="Attacker's STR 28 milestone: damage cannot fall below half"><input type="checkbox" name="overwhelmingForce"> Overwhelming Force</label>
  <fieldset class="wb-dice-choices">
    <legend>Dice</legend>
    <label><input type="radio" name="mode" value="normal" checked> Normal</label>
    <label data-tooltip="Roll two d20s; keep the higher"><input type="radio" name="mode" value="advantage"> Advantage</label>
    <label data-tooltip="Roll two d20s; keep the lower"><input type="radio" name="mode" value="disadvantage"> Disadvantage</label>
  </fieldset>
  {{#if used}}<p class="wb-warning">Used in round {{round}} · reset to correct.</p>{{else}}{{#if combatId}}<p class="wb-dialog-meta">Ready · round {{round}}</p>{{/if}}{{/if}}
  <label class="wb-check-toggle"><input type="checkbox" name="spendReaction" {{#if spendReaction}}checked{{/if}}> Spend 1 reaction ({{reactions}} left)</label>
  <details class="wb-disclosure wb-help"><summary>How Parry works</summary>
    <p>Roll d20 + DEX. Beat the attack total to negate damage and non-magical effects; a tie fails. Natural 20 attacks can be parried. Overwhelming Force keeps damage at half or more.</p>
    <p>Requires DEX 21 and a held weapon or shield. Use once per round against a physical melee or ranged attack you can see. To protect an ally within 1 AP of movement, move in front of the attack. Requirements remain correctable for abilities and equipment.</p>
    <p>Spending a reaction also marks this round's Parry use. Reset Parry use clears the mark without refunding a reaction. Unticked spending makes a practice roll. No AP cost. Movement, Health and effect removal stay manual; Wonder is available from the chat card.</p>
  </details>
</div>
